/-!
# Countably indexed completions cut out by countably many equations are adic-star

If `T` is a closed subset of `Spec A` cut out by the vanishing of countably many elements
`f : ℕ → A`, and the completion of `Spec A` along `T` is countably indexed, in the sense of being
realized by a decreasing sequence `J` of ideals cofinal among the ideals cutting out `T`, then
that completion is adic\*: the ring `Q = lim A ⧸ J n` presenting it is adic and carries a
finitely generated ideal of definition.

## Main results

* `idealSequenceLimit_completeSpace_and_t2Space`: the inverse limit of the quotients of a ring by
  a decreasing sequence of ideals is complete and separated for its limit topology.
* `isAdic_idealSequenceLimit_of_countable_zeroLocus`: the ring-level form of clause (1) of
  Stacks tag 0APW.
* `isAdicStar_countableCompletion`: **clause (1) of Stacks tag 0APW**, the sheaf-level form: the
  completion of `Spec A` along a closed set `T` cut out by countably many equations, presented as
  the colimit of the quotient spectra of a cofinal sequence of ideals, is adic\*.

Clause (2) of Stacks tag 0APW — that the conclusion fails without the countability of the
equations — is Gabber's example: its ring-theoretic halves are in
`AlgebraicGeometry.FormalSpace.CountablyIndexedNotAdicStarExample` and the sheaf-level
statement is `AlgebraicGeometry.FormalSpace.CountablyIndexedNotAdicStarSheaf`.

## Implementation notes

The sheaf-level construction follows the same pattern as
`AlgebraicGeometry.FormalSpace.completionAlongIdeal` of
`AlgebraicGeometry.FormalSpace.AffineCompletionAlongIdeal`, which presents the completion along
the powers of a single ideal: a diagram of quotient spectra indexed by `ℕ`, a proof that its
transition maps are thickenings, and an identification of the colimit with the formal spectrum
of the presenting ring via the finality of the kernel-indexing functor. Two things differ. First
the thickening lemma: for powers of a fixed ideal `I` the kernel of a transition
`A ⧸ Iᵏ ⟶ A ⧸ Iⁿ` is nilpotent by the explicit exponent `k`, whereas here every stage `J' n` of
the cofinal sequence has the *same* zero locus `T`, so an element of `J' n` lies in the radical
of `J' m` by `PrimeSpectrum.zeroLocus_subset_zeroLocus_iff`, which is what
`exists_pow_mem_of_zeroLocus_eq_ideal` records. Second, the ring-level input needs a sequence
that is square-cofinal, which the given sequence need not be; it is obtained as a subsequence
`J ∘ idx` by `exists_squareCofinalReindex`, and `countableCompletionReindexIso` shows that
passing to that subsequence does not change the colimit, the reindexing functor being final. So
the statement is about the completion presented by the *given* sequence, not by the refined one.

The ring-level argument first replaces the given cofinal sequence `J` by a sequence `J'` that is
cofinal, cuts out the same closed set, and satisfies `J' (n + 1) ≤ (J' n) ^ 2`; it then produces,
for some
finite prefix of the equations `f`, an ideal `L` whose topological closure `C` is open (such a
prefix exists because otherwise the equations could never generate an ideal cofinal with the
`J' n`, a combinatorial contradiction). The ring `Q` is then weakly adic with ideal of definition
`C`, and since `C ⧸ (closure (C ^ 2))` is a finite-dimensional vector space over the residue ring
(it is a quotient of a module generated by the finitely many equations in the chosen prefix), the
general finiteness criterion for weakly adic rings produces a finitely generated ideal defining
the same topology.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0APW](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0APW)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open Filter Topology CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.FormalSpace

universe u

/-! ### The limit topology on `IdealSequenceLimit` -/

/-- Evaluation of an element of the inverse limit of the quotients of `A` by a decreasing
sequence of ideals at a given index, as a ring homomorphism to that quotient. -/
def idealSequenceLimitProj {A : Type u} [CommRing A] (J : ℕ → Ideal A)
    (hJ : ∀ n, J (n + 1) ≤ J n) (n : ℕ) :
    IdealSequenceLimit A J hJ →+* A ⧸ J n :=
  (Pi.evalRingHom (fun n => A ⧸ J n) n).comp (IdealSequenceLimit A J hJ).subtype

/-- The evaluation `idealSequenceLimitProj J hJ n x` is the `n`-th component of `x`. -/
theorem idealSequenceLimitProj_apply {A : Type u} [CommRing A] (J : ℕ → Ideal A)
    (hJ : ∀ n, J (n + 1) ≤ J n) (n : ℕ) (x : IdealSequenceLimit A J hJ) :
    idealSequenceLimitProj J hJ n x = x.1 n := rfl

/-- The kernel of the evaluation of the inverse limit at an index is open, the quotients being
discrete. -/
theorem idealSequenceLimit_isOpen_ker {A : Type u} [CommRing A] (J : ℕ → Ideal A)
    (hJ : ∀ n, J (n + 1) ≤ J n) (n : ℕ) :
    @IsOpen (IdealSequenceLimit A J hJ) (idealSequenceLimitTopology A J hJ)
      (RingHom.ker (idealSequenceLimitProj J hJ n) : Set (IdealSequenceLimit A J hJ)) := by
  let : TopologicalSpace (IdealSequenceLimit A J hJ) := idealSequenceLimitTopology A J hJ
  let : ∀ k, TopologicalSpace (A ⧸ J k) := fun _ => ⊥
  let : ∀ k, DiscreteTopology (A ⧸ J k) := fun _ => ⟨rfl⟩
  show IsOpen ((fun x : IdealSequenceLimit A J hJ => x.1 n) ⁻¹' ({0} : Set (A ⧸ J n)))
  exact (isOpen_discrete ({0} : Set (A ⧸ J n))).preimage
    ((continuous_apply n).comp continuous_subtype_val)

/-- The kernel of the evaluation of the inverse limit at an index is closed, the quotients being
discrete. -/
theorem idealSequenceLimit_isClosed_ker {A : Type u} [CommRing A] (J : ℕ → Ideal A)
    (hJ : ∀ n, J (n + 1) ≤ J n) (n : ℕ) :
    @IsClosed (IdealSequenceLimit A J hJ) (idealSequenceLimitTopology A J hJ)
      (RingHom.ker (idealSequenceLimitProj J hJ n) : Set (IdealSequenceLimit A J hJ)) := by
  let : TopologicalSpace (IdealSequenceLimit A J hJ) := idealSequenceLimitTopology A J hJ
  let : ∀ k, TopologicalSpace (A ⧸ J k) := fun _ => ⊥
  let : ∀ k, DiscreteTopology (A ⧸ J k) := fun _ => ⟨rfl⟩
  show IsClosed ((fun x : IdealSequenceLimit A J hJ => x.1 n) ⁻¹' ({0} : Set (A ⧸ J n)))
  exact isClosed_singleton.preimage ((continuous_apply n).comp continuous_subtype_val)

/-- An open set of the inverse limit containing `x` contains every element agreeing with `x` at
one sufficiently large index, the limit topology being induced from the product of discrete
quotients. -/
private theorem exists_forall_proj_eq_mem_of_isOpen {A : Type u} [CommRing A] (J : ℕ → Ideal A)
    (hJ : ∀ n, J (n + 1) ≤ J n) {O : Set (IdealSequenceLimit A J hJ)}
    (hO : @IsOpen _ (idealSequenceLimitTopology A J hJ) O) {x : IdealSequenceLimit A J hJ}
    (hx : x ∈ O) (k₀ : ℕ) :
    ∃ k, k₀ ≤ k ∧ ∀ y : IdealSequenceLimit A J hJ, y.1 k = x.1 k → y ∈ O := by
  let : ∀ n, TopologicalSpace (A ⧸ J n) := fun _ => ⊥
  let : ∀ n, DiscreteTopology (A ⧸ J n) := fun _ => ⟨rfl⟩
  obtain ⟨V, hV, hVO⟩ := isOpen_induced_iff.mp hO
  have hVnhds : V ∈ 𝓝 x.1 := hV.mem_nhds (by rwa [← hVO] at hx)
  rw [nhds_pi, Filter.mem_pi'] at hVnhds
  obtain ⟨s, t, ht, hst⟩ := hVnhds
  refine ⟨max k₀ (s.sup id), le_max_left _ _, fun y hy => ?_⟩
  have hyV : y ∈ Subtype.val ⁻¹' V := hst fun i hi => by
    have hik : i ≤ max k₀ (s.sup id) := (Finset.le_sup (f := id) hi).trans (le_max_right _ _)
    have hyi : y.1 i = x.1 i := by
      calc
        y.1 i = Ideal.Quotient.factor (antitone_nat_of_succ_le hJ hik) (y.1 _) := (y.2 i _ hik).symm
        _ = Ideal.Quotient.factor (antitone_nat_of_succ_le hJ hik) (x.1 _) := by rw [hy]
        _ = x.1 i := x.2 i _ hik
    have hti := ht i
    rw [nhds_discrete] at hti
    rw [hyi]
    exact Filter.mem_pure.mp hti
  rwa [hVO] at hyV

/-- If `x` of the inverse limit vanishes at `m` and `a` lifts its coordinate at `k ≥ m`, then
`a ∈ J m`. -/
private theorem mem_of_proj_eq_zero {A : Type u} [CommRing A] (J : ℕ → Ideal A)
    (hJ : ∀ n, J (n + 1) ≤ J n) {x : IdealSequenceLimit A J hJ} {m k : ℕ} (hmk : m ≤ k)
    (hx : x.1 m = 0) {a : A} (ha : Ideal.Quotient.mk (J k) a = x.1 k) : a ∈ J m := by
  rw [← Ideal.Quotient.eq_zero_iff_mem, ← hx, ← x.2 m k hmk, ← ha]
  simp

/-- The kernels of the evaluations at the indices form a neighbourhood basis of zero in the
inverse limit of the quotients of `A` by a decreasing sequence of ideals: a neighbourhood of zero
constrains only finitely many coordinates, and compatibility propagates the vanishing of the
coordinate at the largest constrained index to all smaller indices. -/
theorem idealSequenceLimit_hasBasis_nhds_zero {A : Type u} [CommRing A] (J : ℕ → Ideal A)
    (hJ : ∀ n, J (n + 1) ≤ J n) :
    (@nhds (IdealSequenceLimit A J hJ) (idealSequenceLimitTopology A J hJ) 0).HasBasis
      (fun _ : ℕ => True)
      (fun n => (RingHom.ker (idealSequenceLimitProj J hJ n) :
        Set (IdealSequenceLimit A J hJ))) := by
  let : TopologicalSpace (IdealSequenceLimit A J hJ) := idealSequenceLimitTopology A J hJ
  refine Filter.HasBasis.mk fun U => ⟨fun hU => ?_, ?_⟩
  · obtain ⟨O, hOU, hOopen, h0O⟩ := mem_nhds_iff.mp hU
    obtain ⟨k, -, hk⟩ := exists_forall_proj_eq_mem_of_isOpen J hJ hOopen h0O 0
    exact ⟨k, trivial, fun x hx => hOU (hk x (RingHom.mem_ker.mp hx))⟩
  · rintro ⟨n, -, hsub⟩
    exact Filter.mem_of_superset
      ((idealSequenceLimit_isOpen_ker J hJ n).mem_nhds (Ideal.zero_mem _)) hsub

/-- The inverse limit of the quotients of a ring by a decreasing sequence of ideals is complete
and separated for the limit topology: a Cauchy sequence stabilizes at each coordinate, and the
compatible family of its stable values is realized by an element of the limit which the sequence
converges to; an element all of whose coordinates vanish is itself zero. Unlike for the inverse
limit of a sequence of rings along a chain of transition maps, no gluing lemma is needed: every
element of the limit already carries the compatibility at every pair of indices, not only
consecutive ones. -/
@[ega "0 7.2.1" "partial"]
theorem idealSequenceLimit_completeSpace_and_t2Space {A : Type u} [CommRing A]
    (J : ℕ → Ideal A) (hJ : ∀ n, J (n + 1) ≤ J n) :
    letI : TopologicalSpace (IdealSequenceLimit A J hJ) := idealSequenceLimitTopology A J hJ
    letI : ∀ n, TopologicalSpace (A ⧸ J n) := fun _ => ⊥
    letI : ∀ n, DiscreteTopology (A ⧸ J n) := fun _ => ⟨rfl⟩
    letI : IsTopologicalRing (IdealSequenceLimit A J hJ) := inferInstance
    @CompleteSpace (IdealSequenceLimit A J hJ)
        (IsTopologicalAddGroup.rightUniformSpace (IdealSequenceLimit A J hJ)) ∧
      T2Space (IdealSequenceLimit A J hJ) := by
  classical
  let : TopologicalSpace (IdealSequenceLimit A J hJ) := idealSequenceLimitTopology A J hJ
  let : ∀ n, TopologicalSpace (A ⧸ J n) := fun _ => ⊥
  let : ∀ n, DiscreteTopology (A ⧸ J n) := fun _ => ⟨rfl⟩
  let : IsTopologicalRing (IdealSequenceLimit A J hJ) := inferInstance
  let : UniformSpace (IdealSequenceLimit A J hJ) :=
    IsTopologicalAddGroup.rightUniformSpace (IdealSequenceLimit A J hJ)
  let : IsUniformAddGroup (IdealSequenceLimit A J hJ) := isUniformAddGroup_of_addCommGroup
  have hker (n : ℕ) : (RingHom.ker (idealSequenceLimitProj J hJ n) :
      Set (IdealSequenceLimit A J hJ)) ∈ nhds 0 :=
    (idealSequenceLimit_hasBasis_nhds_zero J hJ).mem_iff.mpr ⟨n, trivial, Set.Subset.rfl⟩
  refine ⟨?_, ?_⟩
  · have _ : (nhds (0 : IdealSequenceLimit A J hJ)).IsCountablyGenerated :=
      (idealSequenceLimit_hasBasis_nhds_zero J hJ).isCountablyGenerated
    have _ : (uniformity (IdealSequenceLimit A J hJ)).IsCountablyGenerated := by
      rw [uniformity_eq_comap_nhds_zero]
      exact Filter.comap.isCountablyGenerated _ _
    apply UniformSpace.complete_of_cauchySeq_tendsto
    intro u hu
    have heq (n : ℕ) : ∃ N, ∀ k ≥ N, ∀ l ≥ N,
        idealSequenceLimitProj J hJ n (u k) = idealSequenceLimitProj J hJ n (u l) := by
      refine (cauchySeq_iff.mp hu) {z : IdealSequenceLimit A J hJ × IdealSequenceLimit A J hJ |
        idealSequenceLimitProj J hJ n z.1 = idealSequenceLimitProj J hJ n z.2} ?_
      rw [uniformity_eq_comap_nhds_zero]
      refine Filter.mem_comap.mpr
        ⟨RingHom.ker (idealSequenceLimitProj J hJ n), hker n, fun z hz ↦ ?_⟩
      have hz' : idealSequenceLimitProj J hJ n (z.2 - z.1) = 0 := RingHom.mem_ker.mp hz
      rw [map_sub] at hz'
      exact (sub_eq_zero.mp hz').symm
    choose N hN using heq
    let z : IdealSequenceLimit A J hJ :=
      ⟨fun n => idealSequenceLimitProj J hJ n (u (N n)), by
        intro n m hnm
        set p := max (N n) (N m) with hp
        have h1 : idealSequenceLimitProj J hJ n (u p) = idealSequenceLimitProj J hJ n (u (N n)) :=
          hN n p (le_max_left _ _) (N n) le_rfl
        have h2 : idealSequenceLimitProj J hJ m (u p) = idealSequenceLimitProj J hJ m (u (N m)) :=
          hN m p (le_max_right _ _) (N m) le_rfl
        have h3 : Ideal.Quotient.factor (antitone_nat_of_succ_le hJ hnm)
            (idealSequenceLimitProj J hJ m (u p)) = idealSequenceLimitProj J hJ n (u p) :=
          (u p).2 n m hnm
        simpa only [← h1, ← h2] using h3⟩
    refine ⟨z, ?_⟩
    have hsub : Tendsto (fun k : ℕ ↦ u k - z) atTop (nhds (0 : IdealSequenceLimit A J hJ)) := by
      refine (idealSequenceLimit_hasBasis_nhds_zero J hJ).tendsto_right_iff.mpr fun n _ ↦ ?_
      filter_upwards [Filter.eventually_ge_atTop (N n)] with k hk
      have hval : idealSequenceLimitProj J hJ n (u k) = idealSequenceLimitProj J hJ n z :=
        (hN n k hk (N n) le_rfl)
      exact RingHom.mem_ker.mpr (by rw [map_sub, hval, sub_self])
    simpa using hsub.add
      (tendsto_const_nhds : Tendsto (fun _ : ℕ ↦ z) atTop (nhds z))
  · refine IsTopologicalAddGroup.t2Space_of_zero_sep fun a ha ↦ ?_
    have hex : ∃ n, idealSequenceLimitProj J hJ n a ≠ 0 := by
      by_contra h
      push Not at h
      refine ha ?_
      exact Subtype.ext (funext fun n => h n)
    obtain ⟨n, hn⟩ := hex
    exact ⟨RingHom.ker (idealSequenceLimitProj J hJ n), hker n,
      fun hz ↦ hn (RingHom.mem_ker.mp hz)⟩

/-! ### Clause (1): a countably indexed completion cut out by countably many equations is adic -/

/-- If two ideals have the same zero locus then every element of one has a power in the other. -/
private lemma exists_pow_mem_of_zeroLocus_eq_ideal {A : Type u} [CommRing A] (I L : Ideal A)
    (hzero : PrimeSpectrum.zeroLocus (I : Set A) = PrimeSpectrum.zeroLocus (L : Set A)) :
    ∀ x ∈ I, ∃ k : ℕ, x ^ k ∈ L := fun _ hx =>
  Ideal.mem_radical_iff.mp (((PrimeSpectrum.zeroLocus_subset_zeroLocus_iff _ _).mp hzero.ge) hx)

/-- If `L ≤ I` have the same zero locus, the kernel of `A ⧸ L → A ⧸ I` is nilpotent. -/
private lemma ker_factor_le_nilradical {A : Type u} [CommRing A] {I L : Ideal A} (hle : L ≤ I)
    (hzero : PrimeSpectrum.zeroLocus (I : Set A) = PrimeSpectrum.zeroLocus (L : Set A)) :
    RingHom.ker (Ideal.Quotient.factor hle) ≤ nilradical (A ⧸ L) := by
  rw [Ideal.Quotient.factor_ker hle]
  refine Ideal.map_le_iff_le_comap.mpr fun x hx ↦ ?_
  rw [Ideal.mem_comap, mem_nilradical]
  obtain ⟨r, hr⟩ := exists_pow_mem_of_zeroLocus_eq_ideal I L hzero x hx
  refine ⟨r, ?_⟩
  rw [← map_pow]
  exact Ideal.Quotient.eq_zero_iff_mem.mpr hr

/-- A monotone reindexing `idx` of `ℕ` with `n ≤ idx n` pulls a cofinal vanishing sequence back
to a cofinal vanishing sequence: the subsequence still decreases, still cuts out `T`, and is
still cofinal because `J (idx n) ≤ J n`. -/
lemma IsCofinalVanishingSequence.comp_reindex {A : Type u} [CommRing A]
    {T : Set (PrimeSpectrum A)} {J : ℕ → Ideal A} (hJ : IsCofinalVanishingSequence A T J)
    {idx : ℕ → ℕ} (hmono : Monotone idx) (hle : ∀ n, n ≤ idx n) :
    IsCofinalVanishingSequence A T (fun n => J (idx n)) :=
  ⟨fun n => antitone_nat_of_succ_le hJ.1 (hmono (Nat.le_succ n)),
    fun n => hJ.2.1 (idx n),
    fun L hL => by
      obtain ⟨m, hm⟩ := hJ.2.2 L hL
      exact ⟨m, le_trans (antitone_nat_of_succ_le hJ.1 (hle m)) hm⟩⟩

/-- A cofinal vanishing sequence admits a monotone reindexing along which it becomes
square-cofinal. The reindexing is built recursively: at each step one passes both to a strictly
later index and beyond an index at which the sequence drops below the square of the current
stage, such an index existing because the square has the same zero locus and the sequence is
cofinal among the ideals with that zero locus. -/
lemma exists_squareCofinalReindex {A : Type u} [CommRing A] {T : Set (PrimeSpectrum A)}
    (J : ℕ → Ideal A) (hJ : IsCofinalVanishingSequence A T J) :
    ∃ idx : ℕ → ℕ, Monotone idx ∧ (∀ n, n ≤ idx n) ∧
      ∀ n, J (idx (n + 1)) ≤ J (idx n) ^ 2 := by
  let pick (k : ℕ) : ℕ := Classical.choose
    (hJ.2.2 (J k ^ 2) (by
      rw [PrimeSpectrum.zeroLocus_pow (J k) (by norm_num)]
      exact hJ.2.1 k))
  let idx : ℕ → ℕ := Nat.rec 0 (fun _ k => max (k + 1) (pick k))
  have hstep (n : ℕ) : idx (n + 1) = max (idx n + 1) (pick (idx n)) := by
    simp [idx, pick]
  have hidx (n : ℕ) : n ≤ idx n := by
    induction n with
    | zero => simp [idx]
    | succ n ih =>
      rw [hstep n]
      omega
  refine ⟨idx, monotone_nat_of_le_succ fun n => by rw [hstep n]; omega, hidx, fun n => ?_⟩
  rw [hstep n]
  exact le_trans
    (antitone_nat_of_succ_le hJ.1 (le_max_right _ _))
    (Classical.choose_spec (hJ.2.2 (J (idx n) ^ 2) (by
      rw [PrimeSpectrum.zeroLocus_pow (J (idx n)) (by norm_num)]
      exact hJ.2.1 (idx n))))

/-- A cofinal vanishing sequence can be replaced by one that is moreover square-cofinal, in the
sense that `K (n + 1) ≤ (K n) ^ 2`. -/
lemma exists_squareCofinalVanishingSequence
    {A : Type u} [CommRing A] {T : Set (PrimeSpectrum A)}
    (J : ℕ → Ideal A)
    (hJ : IsCofinalVanishingSequence A T J) :
    ∃ K : ℕ → Ideal A,
      (∀ n, K (n + 1) ≤ K n) ∧
      (∀ n, PrimeSpectrum.zeroLocus (K n : Set A) = T) ∧
      (∀ L : Ideal A, PrimeSpectrum.zeroLocus (L : Set A) = T →
        ∃ n, K n ≤ L) ∧
      (∀ n, K (n + 1) ≤ K n ^ 2) := by
  obtain ⟨idx, hmono, hle, hsq⟩ := exists_squareCofinalReindex J hJ
  obtain ⟨hdec, hzero, hcofinal⟩ := hJ.comp_reindex hmono hle
  exact ⟨fun n => J (idx n), hdec, hzero, hcofinal, hsq⟩

private lemma exists_positive_power_sequence
    {A : Type u} [CommRing A] (J : ℕ → Ideal A) (f : ℕ → A)
    (stage : ℕ → ℕ) (hpow : ∀ m n, ∃ k : ℕ, f n ^ k ∈ J m) :
    ∃ e : ℕ → ℕ,
      (∀ n, 0 < e n) ∧
      (∀ n, f n ^ e n ∈ J (stage n)) ∧
      PrimeSpectrum.zeroLocus
          (Set.range fun n => f n ^ e n) =
        PrimeSpectrum.zeroLocus (Set.range f) := by
  classical
  let e (n : ℕ) := (Classical.choose (hpow (stage n) n)) + 1
  refine ⟨e, ?_, ?_, ?_⟩
  · intro n
    exact Nat.succ_pos _
  · intro n
    have hk := Classical.choose_spec (hpow (stage n) n)
    show f n ^ (Classical.choose (hpow (stage n) n) + 1) ∈ J (stage n)
    rw [pow_succ]
    exact Ideal.mul_mem_right (f n) (J (stage n)) hk
  · ext p
    constructor
    · intro hp
      have hp' : Set.range (fun n => f n ^ e n) ⊆ p.asIdeal :=
        (PrimeSpectrum.mem_zeroLocus p _).mp hp
      apply (PrimeSpectrum.mem_zeroLocus p _).mpr
      rintro x ⟨n, rfl⟩
      exact p.2.mem_of_pow_mem (e n) (hp' ⟨n, rfl⟩)
    · intro hp
      have hp' : Set.range f ⊆ p.asIdeal :=
        (PrimeSpectrum.mem_zeroLocus p _).mp hp
      apply (PrimeSpectrum.mem_zeroLocus p _).mpr
      rintro x ⟨n, rfl⟩
      exact (p.2.pow_mem_iff_mem (e n) (by positivity)).2 (hp' ⟨n, rfl⟩)

/-- The diagonal ring homomorphism from `A` to the inverse limit of the quotients `A ⧸ J n`,
sending `a` to the compatible family of its residue classes. -/
noncomputable def idealSequenceLimitDiagonal
    {A : Type u} [CommRing A] (J : ℕ → Ideal A)
    (hJ : ∀ n, J (n + 1) ≤ J n) :
    A →+* IdealSequenceLimit A J hJ :=
  RingHom.codRestrict (RingHom.pi fun n => Ideal.Quotient.mk (J n))
    (IdealSequenceLimit A J hJ) (by
      intro a n m h
      change Ideal.Quotient.factor (antitone_nat_of_succ_le hJ h)
        (Ideal.Quotient.mk (J m) a) = Ideal.Quotient.mk (J n) a
      simp)

/-- Evaluation of the inverse limit at an index is surjective. -/
theorem idealSequenceLimitProj_surjective {A : Type u} [CommRing A] (J : ℕ → Ideal A)
    (hJ : ∀ n, J (n + 1) ≤ J n) (n : ℕ) :
    Function.Surjective (idealSequenceLimitProj J hJ n) := by
  have hcomp : Function.Surjective
      (idealSequenceLimitProj J hJ n ∘ idealSequenceLimitDiagonal J hJ) := by
    intro b
    obtain ⟨a, ha⟩ := Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective b
    exact ⟨a, by
      show (idealSequenceLimitDiagonal J hJ a).1 n = b
      simp [idealSequenceLimitDiagonal, ha]⟩
  exact Function.Surjective.of_comp hcomp

private noncomputable def idealSequenceLimitPrefixIdeal
    {A : Type u} [CommRing A] (J : ℕ → Ideal A)
    (hJ : ∀ n, J (n + 1) ≤ J n) (f : ℕ → A) (m : ℕ) :
    Ideal (IdealSequenceLimit A J hJ) :=
  (Ideal.span (f '' {i | i < m})).map (idealSequenceLimitDiagonal J hJ)

private theorem exists_stage_gap_of_not_open_prefix
    {A : Type u} [CommRing A] (J : ℕ → Ideal A)
    (hJ : ∀ n, J (n + 1) ≤ J n) (f : ℕ → A) (m : ℕ)
    (hnot : ¬ @IsOpen (IdealSequenceLimit A J hJ)
      (idealSequenceLimitTopology A J hJ)
      (@closure (IdealSequenceLimit A J hJ)
        (idealSequenceLimitTopology A J hJ)
        (idealSequenceLimitPrefixIdeal J hJ f m : Set
          (IdealSequenceLimit A J hJ)))) :
    ∃ n, m ≤ n ∧ ¬ J n ≤ Ideal.span (f '' {i | i < m}) ⊔ J (n + 1) := by
  classical
  by_contra hno
  let Q := IdealSequenceLimit A J hJ
  let : TopologicalSpace Q := idealSequenceLimitTopology A J hJ
  let : ∀ n, TopologicalSpace (A ⧸ J n) := fun _ => ⊥
  let : ∀ n, DiscreteTopology (A ⧸ J n) := fun _ => ⟨rfl⟩
  let : IsTopologicalAddGroup (∀ n, A ⧸ J n) := inferInstance
  let : IsTopologicalAddGroup Q := by infer_instance
  let L : Ideal A := Ideal.span (f '' {i | i < m})
  let q : A →+* Q := idealSequenceLimitDiagonal J hJ
  let I : Ideal Q := L.map q
  let U : Set Q := {x | x.1 m = 0}
  have hUopen : IsOpen U := by
    let : TopologicalSpace (A ⧸ J m) := ⊥
    let : DiscreteTopology (A ⧸ J m) := ⟨rfl⟩
    have hc : Continuous (fun x : Q => x.1 m) :=
      (continuous_apply m).comp continuous_subtype_val
    show IsOpen ((fun x : Q => x.1 m) ⁻¹' ({0} : Set (A ⧸ J m)))
    exact (isOpen_discrete ({0} : Set (A ⧸ J m))).preimage hc
  have hgapAll : ∀ n, m ≤ n → J n ≤ L ⊔ J (n + 1) := by
    intro n hmn
    by_contra h
    exact hno ⟨n, hmn, h⟩
  have hiter : ∀ d : ℕ, J m ≤ L ⊔ J (m + d) := by
    intro d
    induction d with
    | zero => exact le_sup_right
    | succ d ih =>
        have hs := hgapAll (m + d) (by omega)
        exact le_trans ih (sup_le le_sup_left hs)
  have hUclosure : U ⊆ closure (I : Set Q) := by
    intro x hx
    rw [mem_closure_iff]
    intro O hO hxO
    obtain ⟨k, hmk, hk⟩ := exists_forall_proj_eq_mem_of_isOpen J hJ hO hxO m
    obtain ⟨a, ha⟩ := Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective (x.1 k)
    have hak : a ∈ L ⊔ J k := by
      have h' := hiter (k - m)
      rw [Nat.add_sub_of_le hmk] at h'
      exact h' (mem_of_proj_eq_zero J hJ hmk hx ha)
    obtain ⟨b, hb, c, hc, hbc⟩ := Submodule.mem_sup.mp hak
    refine ⟨q b, hk _ ?_, Ideal.mem_map_of_mem q hb⟩
    show Ideal.Quotient.mk (J k) b = x.1 k
    rw [← ha]
    apply (Ideal.Quotient.mk_eq_mk_iff_sub_mem b a).2
    rw [← hbc]
    simpa [sub_eq_add_neg] using (J k).neg_mem hc
  have hUnhds : U ∈ 𝓝 (0 : Q) := hUopen.mem_nhds (by simp [U])
  have hclOpen : IsOpen (closure (I : Set Q)) := by
    have hmem : ((I.toAddSubgroup).topologicalClosure : Set Q) ∈ 𝓝 (0 : Q) :=
      Filter.mem_of_superset hUnhds hUclosure
    exact (I.toAddSubgroup.topologicalClosure).isOpen_of_mem_nhds hmem
  exact hnot hclOpen

private lemma no_gap_at_every_finite_prefix
    {A : Type u} [CommRing A] {T : Set (PrimeSpectrum A)}
    (J : ℕ → Ideal A) (f : ℕ → A)
    (hJ : IsCofinalVanishingSequence A T J)
    (hfT : PrimeSpectrum.zeroLocus (Set.range f) = T)
    (hpow : ∀ m n, ∃ k : ℕ, f n ^ k ∈ J m)
    (hgap : ∀ m, ∃ N, m ≤ N ∧
      ¬ J N ≤ Ideal.span (f '' {i | i < m}) ⊔ J (N + 1)) : False := by
  classical
  let phi (m : ℕ) : ℕ := Classical.choose (hgap m)
  have hphi (m : ℕ) : m ≤ phi m := (Classical.choose_spec (hgap m)).1
  let stage : ℕ → ℕ := Nat.rec (phi 0) (fun n k => max k (phi (n + 1)))
  have hstage (m n : ℕ) (hmn : m ≤ n) : phi m ≤ stage n := by
    induction n generalizing m with
    | zero =>
        have : m = 0 := by omega
        subst m
        simp [stage]
    | succ n ih =>
        by_cases h : m = n + 1
        · subst m
          simp [stage]
        · have hm : m ≤ n := by omega
          have := ih m hm
          simp only [stage]
          exact this.trans (le_max_left _ _)
  obtain ⟨e, hepos, heJ, hezero⟩ :=
    exists_positive_power_sequence J f (fun n => stage n + 1) hpow
  let K : Ideal A := Ideal.span (Set.range fun n => f n ^ e n)
  have hKzero : PrimeSpectrum.zeroLocus (K : Set A) = T := by
    dsimp [K]
    rw [PrimeSpectrum.zeroLocus_span, hezero]
    exact hfT
  obtain ⟨n, hnK⟩ := hJ.2.2 K hKzero
  let m := n
  have hbound : K ≤ Ideal.span (f '' {i | i < m}) ⊔ J (phi m + 1) := by
    apply Ideal.span_le.mpr
    rintro x ⟨i, rfl⟩
    by_cases hi : i < m
    · apply Ideal.mem_sup_left
      exact (Ideal.span (f '' {i | i < m})).pow_mem_of_mem
        (Ideal.subset_span ⟨i, hi, rfl⟩) (e i) (hepos i)
    · apply Ideal.mem_sup_right
      have hmi : m ≤ i := by omega
      have hst : phi m + 1 ≤ stage i + 1 := Nat.succ_le_succ (hstage m i hmi)
      exact (antitone_nat_of_succ_le hJ.1 hst) (heJ i)
  obtain ⟨x, hxJ, hxnot⟩ := SetLike.not_le_iff_exists.mp
    (Classical.choose_spec (hgap m)).2
  have hxK : x ∈ K := hnK
    ((antitone_nat_of_succ_le hJ.1 (hphi m)) hxJ)
  exact hxnot (hbound hxK)

/-- The ring-theoretic content of clause (1) of Stacks tag 0APW, for the inverse limit
`Q = lim A ⧸ J' n` of a square-cofinal decreasing sequence of ideals cutting out the zero locus
of countably many equations `f`: `Q` is adic and carries a finitely generated ideal of
definition. Unlike `isAdic_idealSequenceLimit_of_countable_zeroLocus`, the ring `Q` is named
in the conclusion rather than existentially quantified, so that a construction needing to know
the presenting ring itself -- not merely that one exists -- can reuse this argument; this is
what the sheaf-level form of the clause requires. -/
theorem isAdic_and_exists_fg_idealOfDefinition_of_squareCofinal
    {A : Type u} [CommRing A] (J' : ℕ → Ideal A) (hJ'dec : ∀ n, J' (n + 1) ≤ J' n) (f : ℕ → A)
    (hJ'zero : ∀ n, PrimeSpectrum.zeroLocus (J' n : Set A) =
      PrimeSpectrum.zeroLocus (Set.range f))
    (hJ'cofinal : ∀ L : Ideal A, PrimeSpectrum.zeroLocus (L : Set A) =
      PrimeSpectrum.zeroLocus (Set.range f) → ∃ n, J' n ≤ L)
    (hJ'square : ∀ n, J' (n + 1) ≤ J' n ^ 2) :
    letI : TopologicalSpace (IdealSequenceLimit A J' hJ'dec) :=
      idealSequenceLimitTopology A J' hJ'dec
    letI : ∀ n, TopologicalSpace (A ⧸ J' n) := fun _ => ⊥
    letI : ∀ n, DiscreteTopology (A ⧸ J' n) := fun _ => ⟨rfl⟩
    letI : IsTopologicalRing (IdealSequenceLimit A J' hJ'dec) := inferInstance
    TopologicalRing.IsAdic (IdealSequenceLimit A J' hJ'dec) ∧
      ∃ I : Ideal (IdealSequenceLimit A J' hJ'dec),
        TopologicalRing.IsIdealOfDefinition I ∧ I.FG := by
  classical
  let : TopologicalSpace (IdealSequenceLimit A J' hJ'dec) :=
    idealSequenceLimitTopology A J' hJ'dec
  let : ∀ n, TopologicalSpace (A ⧸ J' n) := fun _ => ⊥
  let : ∀ n, DiscreteTopology (A ⧸ J' n) := fun _ => ⟨rfl⟩
  let : CommRing (IdealSequenceLimit A J' hJ'dec) := inferInstance
  let : IsTopologicalRing (IdealSequenceLimit A J' hJ'dec) := inferInstance
  let : IsTopologicalAddGroup (IdealSequenceLimit A J' hJ'dec) := inferInstance
  have hJrange : IsCofinalVanishingSequence A (PrimeSpectrum.zeroLocus (Set.range f)) J' :=
    ⟨hJ'dec, hJ'zero, hJ'cofinal⟩
  have hpow' (m n : ℕ) : ∃ k : ℕ, f n ^ k ∈ J' m :=
    exists_pow_mem_of_zeroLocus_eq_ideal (Ideal.span (Set.range f)) (J' m)
      (by rw [PrimeSpectrum.zeroLocus_span]; exact (hJ'zero m).symm) (f n)
      (Ideal.subset_span ⟨n, rfl⟩)
  let Q := IdealSequenceLimit A J' hJ'dec
  have hsomeOpenPrefix : ∃ m, IsOpen (closure
      (idealSequenceLimitPrefixIdeal J' hJ'dec f m : Set Q)) := by
    by_contra hnone
    apply no_gap_at_every_finite_prefix J' f hJrange rfl hpow'
    intro m
    exact exists_stage_gap_of_not_open_prefix J' hJ'dec f m (by
      intro hopen
      exact hnone ⟨m, hopen⟩)
  obtain ⟨m, hprefixOpen⟩ := hsomeOpenPrefix
  let L : Ideal Q := idealSequenceLimitPrefixIdeal J' hJ'dec f m
  let C : Ideal Q := L.topologicalClosure
  have hCopen : IsOpen (C : Set Q) := by
    show IsOpen (closure (L : Set Q))
    exact hprefixOpen
  let π (n : ℕ) : Q →+* A ⧸ J' n := idealSequenceLimitProj J' hJ'dec n
  let K (n : ℕ) : Ideal Q := RingHom.ker (π n)
  have hKopen (n : ℕ) : IsOpen (K n : Set Q) := idealSequenceLimit_isOpen_ker J' hJ'dec n
  have hKclosed (n : ℕ) : IsClosed (K n : Set Q) := idealSequenceLimit_isClosed_ker J' hJ'dec n
  have hKernelBasis' : (𝓝 (0 : Q)).HasBasis (fun _ : ℕ => True)
      (fun n => (K n : Set Q)) := idealSequenceLimit_hasBasis_nhds_zero J' hJ'dec
  have hKernelBasis (U : Set Q) (hU : U ∈ 𝓝 (0 : Q)) :
      ∃ n, (K n : Set Q) ⊆ U := by
    obtain ⟨n, -, hn⟩ := hKernelBasis'.mem_iff.mp hU
    exact ⟨n, hn⟩
  let : IsLinearTopology Q Q := IsLinearTopology.mk_of_hasBasis' Q hKernelBasis'
    (by intro I r x hx; exact I.smul_mem r hx)
  have hLfg : L.FG := by
    dsimp [L, idealSequenceLimitPrefixIdeal]
    apply Ideal.FG.map
    apply Submodule.fg_span
    exact (Set.finite_lt_nat m).image f
  have hLrad (n : ℕ) : L ≤ (K n).radical := by
    apply Ideal.map_le_iff_le_comap.mpr
    apply Ideal.span_le.mpr
    rintro x ⟨i, hi, rfl⟩
    apply Ideal.mem_radical_iff.mpr
    obtain ⟨k, hk⟩ := hpow' n i
    refine ⟨k, ?_⟩
    show (π n) (idealSequenceLimitDiagonal J' hJ'dec (f i) ^ k) = 0
    rw [map_pow]
    show Ideal.Quotient.mk (J' n) (f i ^ k) = 0
    exact Ideal.Quotient.eq_zero_iff_mem.mpr hk
  have hLpow (n : ℕ) : ∃ r, L ^ r ≤ K n :=
    Ideal.exists_pow_le_of_le_radical_of_fg (hLrad n) hLfg
  have hCpowAux : ∀ r : ℕ, C ^ r ≤ (L ^ r).topologicalClosure := by
    have htop : (⊤ : Ideal Q).topologicalClosure = ⊤ :=
      (isClosed_univ : IsClosed ((⊤ : Ideal Q) : Set Q)).submodule_topologicalClosure_eq
    intro r
    induction r with
    | zero => simp [pow_zero, Ideal.one_eq_top, htop]
    | succ r ih =>
      rw [pow_succ]
      calc
        C ^ r * C ≤ (L ^ r).topologicalClosure * L.topologicalClosure :=
          Ideal.mul_mono ih (show C ≤ L.topologicalClosure by rfl)
        _ ≤ (L ^ r * L).topologicalClosure := TopologicalRing.closure_mul_le _ _
        _ = (L ^ (r + 1)).topologicalClosure := by rw [pow_succ]
  have hCpow_le_kernel (n : ℕ) : ∃ r, C ^ r ≤ K n := by
    obtain ⟨r, hr⟩ := hLpow n
    refine ⟨r, ?_⟩
    exact (hCpowAux r).trans
      (Submodule.topologicalClosure_minimal (L ^ r) hr (hKclosed n))
  have hdiagKernel (j : ℕ) : (K j : Set Q) ⊆
      closure ((idealSequenceLimitDiagonal J' hJ'dec) '' (J' j : Set A)) := by
    intro x hx
    rw [mem_closure_iff]
    intro O hO hxO
    obtain ⟨k, hjk, hk⟩ := exists_forall_proj_eq_mem_of_isOpen J' hJ'dec hO hxO j
    obtain ⟨a, ha⟩ := Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective (x.1 k)
    exact ⟨idealSequenceLimitDiagonal J' hJ'dec a, hk _ ha,
      a, mem_of_proj_eq_zero J' hJ'dec hjk (RingHom.mem_ker.mp hx) ha, rfl⟩
  obtain ⟨N, hNC⟩ := hKernelBasis (C : Set Q) (hCopen.mem_nhds (Ideal.zero_mem C))
  have hdiagN : (Ideal.span (idealSequenceLimitDiagonal J' hJ'dec '' (J' N : Set A))) ≤ C := by
    apply Ideal.span_le.mpr
    rintro x ⟨a, ha, rfl⟩
    exact hNC (Ideal.Quotient.eq_zero_iff_mem.mpr ha)
  have hJiter (d : ℕ) : J' (N + d) ≤ J' N ^ (2 ^ d) := by
    induction d with
    | zero => simp
    | succ d ih =>
        have hindex : N + (d + 1) = (N + d) + 1 := by omega
        calc
          J' (N + (d + 1)) = J' ((N + d) + 1) := by rw [hindex]
          _ ≤ J' (N + d) ^ 2 := hJ'square (N + d)
          _ ≤ (J' N ^ (2 ^ d)) ^ 2 := Ideal.pow_right_mono ih 2
          _ = J' N ^ (2 ^ (d + 1)) := by
            rw [← pow_mul, pow_succ]
  have hkernel_le_closure_Cpow (d : ℕ) :
      K (N + d) ≤ (C ^ (2 ^ d)).topologicalClosure := by
    intro x hx
    have hxcl : x ∈ closure ((idealSequenceLimitDiagonal J' hJ'dec) ''
        (J' (N + d) : Set A)) := hdiagKernel (N + d) hx
    have hset : ((idealSequenceLimitDiagonal J' hJ'dec) ''
        (J' (N + d) : Set A)) ⊆ (C ^ (2 ^ d)).topologicalClosure := by
      rintro y ⟨a, ha, rfl⟩
      have hmapN : (J' N).map (idealSequenceLimitDiagonal J' hJ'dec) ≤ C := hdiagN
      have hmapPow : (J' N ^ (2 ^ d)).map
          (idealSequenceLimitDiagonal J' hJ'dec) ≤ C ^ (2 ^ d) := by
        rw [Ideal.map_pow]
        exact Ideal.pow_right_mono hmapN (2 ^ d)
      have hmapmem : idealSequenceLimitDiagonal J' hJ'dec a ∈
          (J' N ^ (2 ^ d)).map (idealSequenceLimitDiagonal J' hJ'dec) :=
        Ideal.mem_map_of_mem _ (hJiter d ha)
      have hmem : idealSequenceLimitDiagonal J' hJ'dec a ∈
          (C ^ (2 ^ d) : Ideal Q) := hmapPow hmapmem
      exact subset_closure hmem
    exact (closure_minimal hset (Submodule.isClosed_topologicalClosure _)) hxcl
  have hCpowOpen (r : ℕ) : IsOpen ((C ^ r).topologicalClosure : Set Q) := by
    have hsub : K (N + r) ≤ (C ^ r).topologicalClosure :=
      (hkernel_le_closure_Cpow r).trans
        (Submodule.topologicalClosure_mono
          (Ideal.pow_le_pow_right Nat.lt_two_pow_self.le))
    exact Ideal.isOpen_of_isOpen_subideal hsub (hKopen (N + r))
  have hCbasis : (𝓝 (0 : Q)).HasBasis (fun _ : ℕ => True)
      (fun r => ((C ^ r).topologicalClosure : Set Q)) := by
    refine Filter.HasBasis.mk ?_
    intro U
    constructor
    · intro hU
      obtain ⟨n, hn⟩ := hKernelBasis U hU
      obtain ⟨r, hr⟩ := hCpow_le_kernel n
      have hcl : (C ^ r).topologicalClosure ≤ K n := by
        intro x hx
        exact Submodule.topologicalClosure_minimal (C ^ r) hr (hKclosed n) hx
      exact ⟨r, trivial, (SetLike.coe_subset_coe.mpr hcl).trans hn⟩
    · rintro ⟨r, -, hsub⟩
      exact Filter.mem_of_superset
        ((hCpowOpen r).mem_nhds (Ideal.zero_mem _)) hsub
  let : TopologicalRing.IsWeaklyPreAdic Q := ⟨C, hCpowOpen, hCbasis⟩
  have hCdef : TopologicalRing.IsIdealOfDefinition C := by
    refine ⟨hCopen, ?_⟩
    intro U hU
    obtain ⟨n, hn⟩ := hKernelBasis U hU
    obtain ⟨r, hr⟩ := hCpow_le_kernel n
    refine ⟨r, ?_⟩
    exact (SetLike.coe_subset_coe.mpr hr).trans hn
  have hI2open : IsOpen ((C ^ 2).topologicalClosure : Set Q) := hCpowOpen 2
  let p : Submodule Q C :=
    Submodule.comap C.subtype (C ^ 2).topologicalClosure
  let cotangent : Type _ := C ⧸ p
  have hLC : L ≤ C := Submodule.le_topologicalClosure L
  let fromL : L →ₗ[Q] cotangent :=
    (Submodule.mkQ p).comp (Submodule.inclusion hLC)
  have hfromLsurj : Function.Surjective fromL := by
    intro z
    obtain ⟨c, hc⟩ := p.mkQ_surjective z
    let O : Set Q := {x | (c : Q) - x ∈ (C ^ 2).topologicalClosure}
    have hOopen : IsOpen O := by
      show IsOpen ((fun x : Q => (c : Q) - x) ⁻¹'
        ((C ^ 2).topologicalClosure : Set Q))
      exact hI2open.preimage (continuous_const.sub continuous_id)
    have hcO : (c : Q) ∈ O := by simp [O]
    obtain ⟨l, hlO, hlL⟩ :=
      (mem_closure_iff.mp (show (c : Q) ∈ closure (L : Set Q) from c.2))
        O hOopen hcO
    let lC : C := ⟨l, hLC hlL⟩
    have hdiff : c - lC ∈ p := by
      show ((c - lC : C) : Q) ∈ (C ^ 2).topologicalClosure
      exact hlO
    have hquot : Submodule.mkQ p c = Submodule.mkQ p lC :=
      (Submodule.Quotient.eq p).2 hdiff
    refine ⟨⟨l, hlL⟩, ?_⟩
    show Submodule.mkQ p lC = z
    rw [← hc]
    exact hquot.symm
  have hcotangentFinite : Module.Finite Q cotangent := by
    let : Module.Finite Q L := Module.Finite.of_fg hLfg
    exact Module.Finite.of_surjective fromL hfromLsurj
  obtain ⟨hQcomplete, hQT2⟩ := idealSequenceLimit_completeSpace_and_t2Space J' hJ'dec
  let : T2Space Q := hQT2
  let : TopologicalRing.IsWeaklyAdic Q :=
    { toIsWeaklyPreAdic := inferInstance, toT2Space := inferInstance, completeSpace := hQcomplete }
  obtain ⟨JQ, hJQfg, hJQadic⟩ :=
    TopologicalRing.exists_fg_isAdic_of_quotient_closure_sq_finite C hCdef
  have hJQdef : TopologicalRing.IsIdealOfDefinition JQ :=
    ⟨by simpa [pow_one] using (isAdic_iff.mp hJQadic).1 1, (isAdic_iff.mp hJQadic).2⟩
  have hQAdic : TopologicalRing.IsAdic Q :=
    ⟨⟨JQ, hJQdef, hJQadic⟩, ⟨hQT2, hQcomplete⟩⟩
  exact ⟨hQAdic, ⟨JQ, hJQdef, hJQfg⟩⟩

/-- A countably indexed completion along a closed set cut out by countably many equations is
adic, at the level of the ring `Q = lim A ⧸ J n` realizing the completion: the hypotheses are the
countably indexed form of clause (1) of Stacks tag 0APW, and the conclusion gives the two
ring-theoretic ingredients of `IsAdicStar`, namely adicity of `Q` and the existence of a finitely
generated ideal of definition. The sheaf-level form, carrying the `0APW` tag, is
`isAdicStar_countableCompletion` below, which packages this ring together with its presentation
of the completion of `Spec A` along `T` as an fppf sheaf. -/
theorem isAdic_idealSequenceLimit_of_countable_zeroLocus
    {A : Type u} [CommRing A] {T : Set (PrimeSpectrum A)} (J : ℕ → Ideal A)
    (hJ : IsCofinalVanishingSequence A T J) (f : ℕ → A)
    (hfT : T = PrimeSpectrum.zeroLocus (Set.range f)) :
    ∃ (Q : Type u) (_ : CommRing Q) (_ : TopologicalSpace Q) (_ : IsTopologicalRing Q)
      (_ : IsLinearTopology Q Q),
      TopologicalRing.IsAdic Q ∧
        ∃ I : Ideal Q, TopologicalRing.IsIdealOfDefinition I ∧ I.FG := by
  classical
  obtain ⟨J', hJ'dec, hJ'zero, hJ'cofinal, hJ'square⟩ := exists_squareCofinalVanishingSequence J hJ
  have hzero' (m : ℕ) : PrimeSpectrum.zeroLocus (J' m : Set A) =
      PrimeSpectrum.zeroLocus (Set.range f) := by
    rw [hJ'zero m, hfT]
  have hcofinal' : ∀ L : Ideal A, PrimeSpectrum.zeroLocus (L : Set A) =
      PrimeSpectrum.zeroLocus (Set.range f) → ∃ n, J' n ≤ L :=
    fun L hL => hJ'cofinal L (hL.trans hfT.symm)
  obtain ⟨hQAdic, JQ, hJQdef, hJQfg⟩ :=
    isAdic_and_exists_fg_idealOfDefinition_of_squareCofinal J' hJ'dec f hzero' hcofinal' hJ'square
  let : TopologicalSpace (IdealSequenceLimit A J' hJ'dec) :=
    idealSequenceLimitTopology A J' hJ'dec
  let : ∀ n, TopologicalSpace (A ⧸ J' n) := fun _ => ⊥
  let : ∀ n, DiscreteTopology (A ⧸ J' n) := fun _ => ⟨rfl⟩
  let : IsTopologicalRing (IdealSequenceLimit A J' hJ'dec) := inferInstance
  let : IsLinearTopology (IdealSequenceLimit A J' hJ'dec) (IdealSequenceLimit A J' hJ'dec) :=
    IsLinearTopology.mk_of_hasBasis' _ (idealSequenceLimit_hasBasis_nhds_zero J' hJ'dec)
      (fun I r x hx => I.smul_mem r hx)
  exact ⟨IdealSequenceLimit A J' hJ'dec, inferInstance, idealSequenceLimitTopology A J' hJ'dec,
    inferInstance, inferInstance, hQAdic, JQ, hJQdef, hJQfg⟩

/-! ### The limit ring as a linearly topologized ring -/

/-- The inverse limit of the quotients of `A` by a decreasing sequence of ideals is a
topological ring for its limit topology, being a subring of a product of discrete rings. -/
theorem isTopologicalRing_idealSequenceLimit (A : Type u) [CommRing A] (J : ℕ → Ideal A)
    (hJ : ∀ n, J (n + 1) ≤ J n) :
    letI : TopologicalSpace (IdealSequenceLimit A J hJ) := idealSequenceLimitTopology A J hJ
    IsTopologicalRing (IdealSequenceLimit A J hJ) := by
  let : ∀ n, TopologicalSpace (A ⧸ J n) := fun _ => ⊥
  let : ∀ n, DiscreteTopology (A ⧸ J n) := fun _ => ⟨rfl⟩
  let : TopologicalSpace (IdealSequenceLimit A J hJ) := idealSequenceLimitTopology A J hJ
  infer_instance

attribute [local instance] idealSequenceLimitTopology isTopologicalRing_idealSequenceLimit

/-- The limit topology on the inverse limit of a decreasing sequence of ideals is a linear
topology: the kernels of its projections, which form a neighbourhood basis of zero, are
ideals. -/
theorem isLinearTopology_idealSequenceLimit (A : Type u) [CommRing A] (J : ℕ → Ideal A)
    (hJ : ∀ n, J (n + 1) ≤ J n) :
    IsLinearTopology (IdealSequenceLimit A J hJ) (IdealSequenceLimit A J hJ) :=
  IsLinearTopology.mk_of_hasBasis' _ (idealSequenceLimit_hasBasis_nhds_zero J hJ)
    (fun I r _x hx => I.smul_mem r hx)

attribute [local instance] isLinearTopology_idealSequenceLimit

/-! ### The sheaf-level form of clause (1) -/

section Geometry

attribute [local instance] sheaf_hasColimits

variable {A : Type u} [CommRing A]

/-- The kernel of the evaluation of the inverse limit of a decreasing sequence of ideals at a
given index. -/
def countableCompletionKernel (J' : ℕ → Ideal A) (hJ'dec : ∀ n, J' (n + 1) ≤ J' n) (n : ℕ) :
    Ideal (IdealSequenceLimit A J' hJ'dec) :=
  RingHom.ker (idealSequenceLimitProj J' hJ'dec n)

/-- The kernels `countableCompletionKernel J' hJ'dec n` decrease as `n` increases. -/
theorem countableCompletionKernel_antitone (J' : ℕ → Ideal A)
    (hJ'dec : ∀ n, J' (n + 1) ≤ J' n) : Antitone (countableCompletionKernel J' hJ'dec) := by
  intro n m hnm x hx
  have hx0 : x.1 m = 0 := RingHom.mem_ker.mp hx
  have h := x.2 n m hnm
  rw [hx0, map_zero] at h
  exact RingHom.mem_ker.mpr h.symm

/-- The kernel of the evaluation at an index of the inverse limit of a decreasing sequence of
ideals, all cutting out the same closed set `T`, is a weak ideal of definition. -/
theorem isWeakIdealOfDefinition_countableCompletionKernel {T : Set (PrimeSpectrum A)}
    (J' : ℕ → Ideal A) (hJ'dec : ∀ n, J' (n + 1) ≤ J' n)
    (hJ'zero : ∀ n, PrimeSpectrum.zeroLocus (J' n : Set A) = T) (n : ℕ) :
    TopologicalRing.IsWeakIdealOfDefinition (countableCompletionKernel J' hJ'dec n) := by
  refine ⟨idealSequenceLimit_isOpen_ker J' hJ'dec n, fun x hx ↦ ?_⟩
  have hx0 : x.1 n = 0 := RingHom.mem_ker.mp hx
  have hcoordNil : ∀ k : ℕ, ∃ r : ℕ, (x.1 k) ^ r = 0 := by
    intro k
    rcases le_total k n with hkn | hnk
    · refine ⟨1, ?_⟩
      have hfac := x.2 k n hkn
      rw [hx0, map_zero] at hfac
      rw [pow_one, ← hfac]
    · refine ker_factor_le_nilradical (antitone_nat_of_succ_le hJ'dec hnk)
        ((hJ'zero n).trans (hJ'zero k).symm) (RingHom.mem_ker.mpr ?_)
      rw [← hx0]
      exact x.2 n k hnk
  rw [IsTopologicallyNilpotent, (idealSequenceLimit_hasBasis_nhds_zero J' hJ'dec).tendsto_right_iff]
  intro j _
  obtain ⟨r, hr⟩ := hcoordNil j
  refine Filter.eventually_atTop.2 ⟨r, fun m hm ↦ ?_⟩
  refine RingHom.mem_ker.mpr ?_
  rw [idealSequenceLimitProj_apply]
  have hpow : (x ^ m).1 j = (x.1 j) ^ m := rfl
  rw [hpow]
  obtain ⟨d, rfl⟩ := Nat.exists_eq_add_of_le hm
  rw [pow_add, hr, zero_mul]

/-- Every weak ideal of definition of the inverse limit of a decreasing sequence of ideals
contains one of the kernels of its projections, since those kernels form a neighbourhood basis
of zero. -/
theorem exists_countableCompletionKernel_le (J' : ℕ → Ideal A)
    (hJ'dec : ∀ n, J' (n + 1) ≤ J' n) (L : Ideal (IdealSequenceLimit A J' hJ'dec))
    (hL : IsOpen (L : Set (IdealSequenceLimit A J' hJ'dec))) :
    ∃ n, countableCompletionKernel J' hJ'dec n ≤ L := by
  obtain ⟨n, -, hn⟩ := (idealSequenceLimit_hasBasis_nhds_zero J' hJ'dec).mem_iff.mp
    (hL.mem_nhds (Ideal.zero_mem _))
  exact ⟨n, hn⟩

/-- The diagram of quotients of `Spec A` by a countable decreasing sequence of ideals all
cutting out the same closed set: the `n`-th stage is `Spec (A ⧸ J' n)` and the transitions are
the canonical closed immersions coming from the inclusions `J' (n + 1) ≤ J' n`. Unlike
`infinitesimalNeighbourhoodDiagram`, no shift of the index is needed. -/
def countableNeighbourhoodDiagram (B : BigFppfSite.{u}) (S : Scheme.{u}) (hS : B.Contains S)
    (f : Spec (.of A) ⟶ S) (hA : B.Contains (Spec (.of A))) (J' : ℕ → Ideal A)
    (hJ'dec : ∀ n, J' (n + 1) ≤ J' n) : ULift.{u + 1} ℕ ⥤ BigAffineFppf B S hS where
  obj n := quotientOver B S hS f hA (J' n.down)
  map {n m} g := quotientOverTransition B S hS f hA
    (antitone_nat_of_succ_le hJ'dec (show n ≤ m from leOfHom g))
  map_id _ := quotientOverTransition_id B S hS f hA _ _
  map_comp _ _ := (quotientOverTransition_comp B S hS f hA _ _).symm

/-- The completion of `Spec A` along a closed set `T`, presented by a countable decreasing
sequence of ideals cofinal among those cutting out `T`: the colimit, in fppf sheaves over `S`,
of the quotients `Spec (A ⧸ J' n)`. -/
def countableCompletion (B : BigFppfSite.{u}) (S : Scheme.{u}) (hS : B.Contains S)
    (f : Spec (.of A) ⟶ S) (hA : B.Contains (Spec (.of A))) (J' : ℕ → Ideal A)
    (hJ'dec : ∀ n, J' (n + 1) ≤ J' n) : FppfSheaf B S hS :=
  colimit (countableNeighbourhoodDiagram B S hS f hA J' hJ'dec ⋙
    BigAffineFppf.inclusion B S hS ⋙ Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda (BigFppfOver.topology B S hS))

private theorem isThickening_countableNeighbourhood_map (B : BigFppfSite.{u}) (S : Scheme.{u})
    (hS : B.Contains S) (f : Spec (.of A) ⟶ S) (hA : B.Contains (Spec (.of A)))
    {T : Set (PrimeSpectrum A)} (J' : ℕ → Ideal A) (hJ'dec : ∀ n, J' (n + 1) ≤ J' n)
    (hJ'zero : ∀ n, PrimeSpectrum.zeroLocus (J' n : Set A) = T) {n m : ULift.{u + 1} ℕ}
    (g : n ⟶ m) :
    Stacks.Thickenings.IsThickening ((BigAffineFppf.toScheme B S hS).map
      ((countableNeighbourhoodDiagram B S hS f hA J' hJ'dec).map g)) := by
  have hd : n ≤ m := leOfHom g
  have hle : J' m.down ≤ J' n.down := antitone_nat_of_succ_le hJ'dec hd
  let q := Ideal.Quotient.factor hle
  have hker : RingHom.ker q ≤ nilradical (A ⧸ J' m.down) :=
    ker_factor_le_nilradical hle ((hJ'zero n.down).trans (hJ'zero m.down).symm)
  have hqSurj : Function.Surjective q := Ideal.Quotient.factor_surjective hle
  have hsurj : Function.Surjective (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom q)).base := by
    show Function.Surjective (PrimeSpectrum.comap q)
    intro p
    refine ⟨⟨p.asIdeal.map q, Ideal.map_isPrime_of_surjective hqSurj
      (hker.trans (nilradical_le_prime p.asIdeal))⟩, ?_⟩
    apply PrimeSpectrum.ext
    show (p.asIdeal.map q).comap q = p.asIdeal
    rw [Ideal.comap_map_of_surjective q hqSurj p.asIdeal, ← RingHom.ker_eq_comap_bot,
      sup_eq_left.mpr (hker.trans (nilradical_le_prime p.asIdeal))]
  show Stacks.Thickenings.IsThickening (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom q))
  exact ⟨IsClosedImmersion.spec_of_surjective (CommRingCat.ofHom q) hqSurj, hsurj⟩

/-- The completion of `Spec A` along `T`, presented by a countable cofinal sequence of ideals,
satisfies the set-theoretic condition of Stacks 0AIS, the colimit defining it being
countable. -/
theorem satisfiesSetTheoreticCondition_countableCompletion (B : BigFppfSite.{u})
    (S : Scheme.{u}) (hS : B.Contains S) (f : Spec (.of A) ⟶ S) (hA : B.Contains (Spec (.of A)))
    {T : Set (PrimeSpectrum A)} (J' : ℕ → Ideal A) (hJ'dec : ∀ n, J' (n + 1) ≤ J' n)
    (hJ'zero : ∀ n, PrimeSpectrum.zeroLocus (J' n : Set A) = T) :
    SatisfiesSetTheoreticCondition B S hS (countableCompletion B S hS f hA J' hJ'dec) :=
  satisfiesSetTheoreticCondition_of_countable_colimit B S hS
    (countableNeighbourhoodDiagram B S hS f hA J' hJ'dec)
    (fun _ _ g ↦ isThickening_countableNeighbourhood_map B S hS f hA J' hJ'dec hJ'zero g)
    _ ⟨Iso.refl _⟩

/-- **The completion does not change when the presenting sequence is passed to a subsequence.**
A monotone reindexing `idx` of `ℕ` with `n ≤ idx n` induces a final functor of the index
category, so the colimit over the reindexed stages is the colimit over all of them: the
neighbourhood diagram of the subsequence `n ↦ J (idx n)` is literally the composite of the
reindexing functor with the neighbourhood diagram of `J`. -/
def countableCompletionReindexIso (B : BigFppfSite.{u}) (S : Scheme.{u}) (hS : B.Contains S)
    (f : Spec (.of A) ⟶ S) (hA : B.Contains (Spec (.of A))) (J : ℕ → Ideal A)
    (hJdec : ∀ n, J (n + 1) ≤ J n) {idx : ℕ → ℕ} (hmono : Monotone idx)
    (hle : ∀ n, n ≤ idx n) (hdec : ∀ n, J (idx (n + 1)) ≤ J (idx n)) :
    countableCompletion B S hS f hA (fun n => J (idx n)) hdec ≅
      countableCompletion B S hS f hA J hJdec :=
  have hmono' : Monotone fun n : ULift.{u + 1} ℕ => ULift.up.{u + 1} (idx n.down) :=
    fun _ _ h => hmono h
  haveI : hmono'.functor.Final := hmono'.final_functor_iff.mpr fun n => ⟨n, hle n.down⟩
  Functor.Final.colimitIso hmono'.functor
    (countableNeighbourhoodDiagram B S hS f hA J hJdec ⋙
      BigAffineFppf.inclusion B S hS ⋙ Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda (BigFppfOver.topology B S hS))

end Geometry

/-! ### Comparison with the formal spectrum of the inverse limit -/

section Comparison

attribute [local instance] sheaf_hasColimits

variable {A : Type u} [CommRing A]

/-- The quotient of the inverse limit of a decreasing sequence of ideals by the kernel of its
`n`-th projection is the quotient `A ⧸ J' n`. -/
def countableCompletionQuotientEquiv (J' : ℕ → Ideal A) (hJ'dec : ∀ n, J' (n + 1) ≤ J' n)
    (n : ℕ) :
    IdealSequenceLimit A J' hJ'dec ⧸ countableCompletionKernel J' hJ'dec n ≃+* A ⧸ J' n :=
  RingHom.quotientKerEquivOfSurjective (idealSequenceLimitProj_surjective J' hJ'dec n)

private theorem countableCompletionQuotientEquiv_mk (J' : ℕ → Ideal A)
    (hJ'dec : ∀ n, J' (n + 1) ≤ J' n) (n : ℕ) (x : IdealSequenceLimit A J' hJ'dec) :
    countableCompletionQuotientEquiv J' hJ'dec n (Ideal.Quotient.mk _ x) =
      idealSequenceLimitProj J' hJ'dec n x :=
  RingHom.quotientKerEquivOfSurjective_apply_mk (idealSequenceLimitProj_surjective J' hJ'dec n) x

private theorem countableCompletionQuotientEquiv_comp_mk_comp_diagonal (J' : ℕ → Ideal A)
    (hJ'dec : ∀ n, J' (n + 1) ≤ J' n) (n : ℕ) :
    ((countableCompletionQuotientEquiv J' hJ'dec n).toRingHom.comp
        (Ideal.Quotient.mk (countableCompletionKernel J' hJ'dec n))).comp
      (idealSequenceLimitDiagonal J' hJ'dec) = Ideal.Quotient.mk (J' n) := by
  refine RingHom.ext fun a ↦ ?_
  show countableCompletionQuotientEquiv J' hJ'dec n
    (Ideal.Quotient.mk _ (idealSequenceLimitDiagonal J' hJ'dec a)) = _
  rw [countableCompletionQuotientEquiv_mk]
  show (idealSequenceLimitDiagonal J' hJ'dec a).1 n = Ideal.Quotient.mk (J' n) a
  simp [idealSequenceLimitDiagonal]

/-- The inverse limit of a decreasing sequence of ideals of `A` all cutting out the same closed
set `T`, with its limit topology, presented as a topological ring over `S`: the spectrum of
each of its quotients by a weak ideal of definition lies in the site and carries the structure
morphism induced by `Spec A ⟶ S`. -/
def countableCompletionQuotientSystem (B : BigFppfSite.{u}) (S : Scheme.{u}) (hS : B.Contains S)
    (f : Spec (.of A) ⟶ S) (hA : B.Contains (Spec (.of A))) (J' : ℕ → Ideal A)
    (hJ'dec : ∀ n, J' (n + 1) ≤ J' n) :
    QuotientSystem B S hS (IdealSequenceLimit A J' hJ'dec) where
  inSite := by
    intro L
    obtain ⟨n, hker⟩ := exists_countableCompletionKernel_le J' hJ'dec L.1 L.2.1
    let g : A ⧸ J' n →+* IdealSequenceLimit A J' hJ'dec ⧸ L.1 :=
      Ideal.Quotient.lift (J' n)
        ((Ideal.Quotient.mk L.1).comp (idealSequenceLimitDiagonal J' hJ'dec)) (by
          intro a ha
          refine Ideal.Quotient.eq_zero_iff_mem.mpr (hker ?_)
          refine RingHom.mem_ker.mpr ?_
          rw [idealSequenceLimitProj_apply]
          change (idealSequenceLimitDiagonal J' hJ'dec a).1 n = 0
          simpa [idealSequenceLimitDiagonal] using
            (Ideal.Quotient.eq_zero_iff_mem (I := J' n)).mpr ha)
    have hgsurj : Function.Surjective g := by
      intro z
      obtain ⟨c, hc⟩ := Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective z
      obtain ⟨a, ha⟩ := Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective (idealSequenceLimitProj J' hJ'dec n c)
      refine ⟨Ideal.Quotient.mk (J' n) a, ?_⟩
      rw [Ideal.Quotient.lift_mk, ← hc]
      refine (Ideal.Quotient.mk_eq_mk_iff_sub_mem _ _).2 ?_
      have hof : idealSequenceLimitProj J' hJ'dec n (idealSequenceLimitDiagonal J' hJ'dec a) =
          Ideal.Quotient.mk (J' n) a := by
        rw [idealSequenceLimitProj_apply]
        simp [idealSequenceLimitDiagonal]
      have hdiff : c - idealSequenceLimitDiagonal J' hJ'dec a ∈ L.1 := by
        refine hker (RingHom.mem_ker.mpr ?_)
        change idealSequenceLimitProj J' hJ'dec n (c - idealSequenceLimitDiagonal J' hJ'dec a)
          = 0
        rw [map_sub, hof, ← ha, sub_self]
      simpa [neg_sub] using L.1.neg_mem hdiff
    let _ : IsClosedImmersion (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom g)) :=
      IsClosedImmersion.spec_of_surjective _ hgsurj
    exact Scheme.size_lt_of_isClosedImmersion (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom g))
      (contains_spec_quotient B hA (J' n))
  overS := fun L ↦
    Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (Ideal.Quotient.mk L.1)) ≫
      Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (idealSequenceLimitDiagonal J' hJ'dec)) ≫ f
  compatible := by
    intro L M h
    have hstage : Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (Ideal.Quotient.factor h)) ≫
        Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (Ideal.Quotient.mk L.1)) =
        Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (Ideal.Quotient.mk M.1)) := by
      rw [← Spec.map_comp, ← CommRingCat.ofHom_comp, Ideal.Quotient.factor_comp_mk]
    exact congrArg (fun k ↦ k ≫
      Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (idealSequenceLimitDiagonal J' hJ'dec)) ≫ f) hstage

/-- The kernels of the projections of the inverse limit of a decreasing sequence of ideals, as
a monotone map from `ULift ℕ` to the weak ideals of definition ordered by reverse inclusion. -/
def countableCompletionKernelIndex {T : Set (PrimeSpectrum A)} (J' : ℕ → Ideal A)
    (hJ'dec : ∀ n, J' (n + 1) ≤ J' n)
    (hJ'zero : ∀ n, PrimeSpectrum.zeroLocus (J' n : Set A) = T) :
    ULift.{u + 1} ℕ →o WeakIdeals (IdealSequenceLimit A J' hJ'dec) where
  toFun n := ⟨countableCompletionKernel J' hJ'dec n.down,
    isWeakIdealOfDefinition_countableCompletionKernel J' hJ'dec hJ'zero n.down⟩
  monotone' _ _ h :=
    countableCompletionKernel_antitone J' hJ'dec (show _ ≤ _ from h)

/-- The kernels of the projections are cofinal among the weak ideals of definition of the
inverse limit of a decreasing sequence of ideals, so the functor they induce on index
categories is final. -/
theorem final_countableCompletionKernelIndex {T : Set (PrimeSpectrum A)} (J' : ℕ → Ideal A)
    (hJ'dec : ∀ n, J' (n + 1) ≤ J' n)
    (hJ'zero : ∀ n, PrimeSpectrum.zeroLocus (J' n : Set A) = T) :
    (countableCompletionKernelIndex J' hJ'dec hJ'zero).monotone.functor.Final := by
  refine (countableCompletionKernelIndex J' hJ'dec hJ'zero).monotone.final_functor_iff.mpr
    fun L ↦ ?_
  obtain ⟨n, hn⟩ := exists_countableCompletionKernel_le J' hJ'dec L.1 L.2.1
  exact ⟨ULift.up n, hn⟩

/-- The `n`-th quotient stage of the completion is the quotient spectrum of the inverse limit
by the kernel of its `n`-th projection. -/
def countableKernelStageIso (B : BigFppfSite.{u}) (S : Scheme.{u}) (hS : B.Contains S)
    (f : Spec (.of A) ⟶ S) (hA : B.Contains (Spec (.of A))) {T : Set (PrimeSpectrum A)}
    (J' : ℕ → Ideal A) (hJ'dec : ∀ n, J' (n + 1) ≤ J' n)
    (hJ'zero : ∀ n, PrimeSpectrum.zeroLocus (J' n : Set A) = T) (n : ULift.{u + 1} ℕ) :
    (countableNeighbourhoodDiagram B S hS f hA J' hJ'dec).obj n ≅
      ((countableCompletionKernelIndex J' hJ'dec hJ'zero).monotone.functor ⋙
        (countableCompletionQuotientSystem B S hS f hA J' hJ'dec).diagram).obj n :=
  ObjectProperty.isoMk _ <| Over.isoMk
    (ObjectProperty.isoMk _ (Scheme.Spec.mapIso
      (countableCompletionQuotientEquiv J' hJ'dec n.down).toCommRingCatIso.op)) (by
    apply ObjectProperty.hom_ext
    change Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom
        (countableCompletionQuotientEquiv J' hJ'dec n.down).toRingHom) ≫
        (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom
          (Ideal.Quotient.mk (countableCompletionKernel J' hJ'dec n.down))) ≫
          Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (idealSequenceLimitDiagonal J' hJ'dec)) ≫ f) =
      Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (Ideal.Quotient.mk (J' n.down))) ≫ f
    rw [← Category.assoc, ← Category.assoc, ← Spec.map_comp, ← Spec.map_comp,
      ← CommRingCat.ofHom_comp, ← CommRingCat.ofHom_comp]
    exact congrArg (fun k ↦ Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom k) ≫ f)
      (countableCompletionQuotientEquiv_comp_mk_comp_diagonal J' hJ'dec n.down))

/-- The identifications of the quotient stages with the quotient spectra of the inverse limit
commute with the transition morphisms. -/
theorem countableKernelStageIso_naturality (B : BigFppfSite.{u}) (S : Scheme.{u})
    (hS : B.Contains S)
    (f : Spec (.of A) ⟶ S) (hA : B.Contains (Spec (.of A))) {T : Set (PrimeSpectrum A)}
    (J' : ℕ → Ideal A) (hJ'dec : ∀ n, J' (n + 1) ≤ J' n)
    (hJ'zero : ∀ n, PrimeSpectrum.zeroLocus (J' n : Set A) = T) {n m : ULift.{u + 1} ℕ}
    (g : n ⟶ m) :
    (countableNeighbourhoodDiagram B S hS f hA J' hJ'dec).map g ≫
        (countableKernelStageIso B S hS f hA J' hJ'dec hJ'zero m).hom =
      (countableKernelStageIso B S hS f hA J' hJ'dec hJ'zero n).hom ≫
        ((countableCompletionKernelIndex J' hJ'dec hJ'zero).monotone.functor ⋙
          (countableCompletionQuotientSystem B S hS f hA J' hJ'dec).diagram).map g := by
  have hd : n ≤ m := leOfHom g
  have hle : J' m.down ≤ J' n.down := antitone_nat_of_succ_le hJ'dec hd
  have hK : countableCompletionKernel J' hJ'dec m.down ≤
      countableCompletionKernel J' hJ'dec n.down :=
    countableCompletionKernel_antitone J' hJ'dec hd
  apply ObjectProperty.hom_ext
  apply Over.OverMorphism.ext
  apply ObjectProperty.hom_ext
  show Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (Ideal.Quotient.factor hle)) ≫
      Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom
        (countableCompletionQuotientEquiv J' hJ'dec m.down).toRingHom) =
    Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom
        (countableCompletionQuotientEquiv J' hJ'dec n.down).toRingHom) ≫
      Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (Ideal.Quotient.factor hK))
  rw [← Spec.map_comp, ← Spec.map_comp, ← CommRingCat.ofHom_comp,
    ← CommRingCat.ofHom_comp, Spec.map_inj]
  apply CommRingCat.hom_ext
  refine RingHom.ext fun y ↦ ?_
  obtain ⟨c, rfl⟩ := Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective y
  show Ideal.Quotient.factor hle (countableCompletionQuotientEquiv J' hJ'dec m.down
      (Ideal.Quotient.mk _ c)) =
    countableCompletionQuotientEquiv J' hJ'dec n.down
      (Ideal.Quotient.factor hK (Ideal.Quotient.mk _ c))
  rw [countableCompletionQuotientEquiv_mk, Ideal.Quotient.factor_mk,
    countableCompletionQuotientEquiv_mk]
  exact c.2 n.down m.down hd

/-- The diagram of quotient spectra of a countable cofinal sequence of ideals is the diagram of
quotient spectra of the inverse limit along the kernels of its projections. -/
def countableNeighbourhoodDiagramIso (B : BigFppfSite.{u}) (S : Scheme.{u}) (hS : B.Contains S)
    (f : Spec (.of A) ⟶ S) (hA : B.Contains (Spec (.of A))) {T : Set (PrimeSpectrum A)}
    (J' : ℕ → Ideal A) (hJ'dec : ∀ n, J' (n + 1) ≤ J' n)
    (hJ'zero : ∀ n, PrimeSpectrum.zeroLocus (J' n : Set A) = T) :
    countableNeighbourhoodDiagram B S hS f hA J' hJ'dec ≅
      (countableCompletionKernelIndex J' hJ'dec hJ'zero).monotone.functor ⋙
        (countableCompletionQuotientSystem B S hS f hA J' hJ'dec).diagram :=
  NatIso.ofComponents (countableKernelStageIso B S hS f hA J' hJ'dec hJ'zero)
    (fun g ↦ countableKernelStageIso_naturality B S hS f hA J' hJ'dec hJ'zero g)

/-- **Stacks 0APW, comparison.** The completion of `Spec A` along `T`, presented by a countable
cofinal sequence of ideals, is the formal spectrum of the inverse limit `Q = lim A ⧸ J' n`: the
kernels of the projections of `Q` are cofinal among its weak ideals of definition, and the
corresponding quotient spectra are the stages of the completion. -/
def countableCompletionIsoFormalSpectrum (B : BigFppfSite.{u}) (S : Scheme.{u})
    (hS : B.Contains S) (f : Spec (.of A) ⟶ S) (hA : B.Contains (Spec (.of A)))
    {T : Set (PrimeSpectrum A)} (J' : ℕ → Ideal A) (hJ'dec : ∀ n, J' (n + 1) ≤ J' n)
    (hJ'zero : ∀ n, PrimeSpectrum.zeroLocus (J' n : Set A) = T) :
    countableCompletion B S hS f hA J' hJ'dec ≅
      formalSpectrum (countableCompletionQuotientSystem B S hS f hA J' hJ'dec) :=
  letI : (countableCompletionKernelIndex J' hJ'dec hJ'zero).monotone.functor.Final :=
    final_countableCompletionKernelIndex J' hJ'dec hJ'zero
  HasColimit.isoOfNatIso (Functor.isoWhiskerRight
      (countableNeighbourhoodDiagramIso B S hS f hA J' hJ'dec hJ'zero)
      (BigAffineFppf.inclusion B S hS ⋙
        Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda (BigFppfOver.topology B S hS))) ≪≫
    Functor.Final.colimitIso (countableCompletionKernelIndex J' hJ'dec hJ'zero).monotone.functor
      (formalSpectrumDiagram (countableCompletionQuotientSystem B S hS f hA J' hJ'dec))

/-- The inverse limit of a countable cofinal sequence of ideals presents the completion of
`Spec A` along `T` as the colimit of the spectra of its quotients by weak ideals of
definition. -/
def countableCompletionWeakIdealPresentation (B : BigFppfSite.{u}) (S : Scheme.{u})
    (hS : B.Contains S) (f : Spec (.of A) ⟶ S) (hA : B.Contains (Spec (.of A)))
    {T : Set (PrimeSpectrum A)} (J' : ℕ → Ideal A) (hJ'dec : ∀ n, J' (n + 1) ≤ J' n)
    (hJ'zero : ∀ n, PrimeSpectrum.zeroLocus (J' n : Set A) = T) :
    WeakIdealColimitPresentation B S hS (IdealSequenceLimit A J' hJ'dec)
      (countableCompletion B S hS f hA J' hJ'dec) where
  diagram := (countableCompletionQuotientSystem B S hS f hA J' hJ'dec).diagram
  quotientIso _ := Iso.refl _
  quotientIso_natural _ _ _ := (Category.comp_id _).trans (Category.id_comp _).symm
  colimitIso := countableCompletionIsoFormalSpectrum B S hS f hA J' hJ'dec hJ'zero

/-- The inverse limit of a countable decreasing sequence of ideals all cutting out the same
closed set, with its limit topology, is weakly admissible: the kernel of the projection to its
`0`-th stage is a weak ideal of definition, and the ring is complete and separated. -/
theorem isWeaklyAdmissible_countableCompletion {T : Set (PrimeSpectrum A)} (J' : ℕ → Ideal A)
    (hJ'dec : ∀ n, J' (n + 1) ≤ J' n)
    (hJ'zero : ∀ n, PrimeSpectrum.zeroLocus (J' n : Set A) = T) :
    TopologicalRing.IsWeaklyAdmissible (IdealSequenceLimit A J' hJ'dec) := by
  obtain ⟨hcs, ht2⟩ := idealSequenceLimit_completeSpace_and_t2Space J' hJ'dec
  exact ⟨⟨countableCompletionKernel J' hJ'dec 0,
      isWeakIdealOfDefinition_countableCompletionKernel J' hJ'dec hJ'zero 0⟩, hcs, ht2⟩

end Comparison

section CountableCase

attribute [local instance] sheaf_hasColimits

variable {A : Type u} [CommRing A]

/-- A presentation of a sheaf as the colimit of the quotient spectra of a topological ring
transports along an isomorphism of sheaves. -/
private def transferWeakIdealColimitPresentation (B : BigFppfSite.{u}) (S : Scheme.{u})
    (hS : B.Contains S) (Q : Type u) [CommRing Q] [TopologicalSpace Q]
    {X Y : FppfSheaf B S hS} (P : WeakIdealColimitPresentation B S hS Q X) (h : Y ≅ X) :
    WeakIdealColimitPresentation B S hS Q Y where
  diagram := P.diagram
  quotientIso := P.quotientIso
  quotientIso_natural := P.quotientIso_natural
  colimitIso := h ≪≫ P.colimitIso

/-- The sheaf-level form of clause (1) of Stacks 0APW for a sheaf identified with the completion
presented by a square-cofinal sequence: the inverse limit `Q = lim A ⧸ J' n` is adic with a
finitely generated ideal of definition by the ring-level clause (1), and presents the sheaf as
the colimit of the spectra of its quotients by weak ideals of definition. -/
theorem isAdicStar_of_squareCofinal (B : BigFppfSite.{u}) (S : Scheme.{u}) (hS : B.Contains S)
    (f : Spec (.of A) ⟶ S) (hA : B.Contains (Spec (.of A))) {T : Set (PrimeSpectrum A)}
    (J' : ℕ → Ideal A) (hJ'dec : ∀ n, J' (n + 1) ≤ J' n)
    (hJ'zero : ∀ n, PrimeSpectrum.zeroLocus (J' n : Set A) = T)
    (hJ'cofinal : ∀ L : Ideal A, PrimeSpectrum.zeroLocus (L : Set A) = T → ∃ n, J' n ≤ L)
    (hJ'square : ∀ n, J' (n + 1) ≤ J' n ^ 2) (e : ℕ → A)
    (heT : T = PrimeSpectrum.zeroLocus (Set.range e)) (X : FppfSheaf B S hS)
    (hX : SatisfiesSetTheoreticCondition B S hS X)
    (iso : X ≅ countableCompletion B S hS f hA J' hJ'dec) :
    IsAdicStar B S hS X := by
  obtain ⟨hQAdic, JQ, hJQdef, hJQfg⟩ :=
    isAdic_and_exists_fg_idealOfDefinition_of_squareCofinal J' hJ'dec e
      (fun n => (hJ'zero n).trans heT)
      (fun L hL => hJ'cofinal L (hL.trans heT.symm)) hJ'square
  have hwa : TopologicalRing.IsWeaklyAdmissible (IdealSequenceLimit A J' hJ'dec) :=
    isWeaklyAdmissible_countableCompletion J' hJ'dec hJ'zero
  have pres : WeakIdealColimitPresentation B S hS (IdealSequenceLimit A J' hJ'dec) X :=
    transferWeakIdealColimitPresentation B S hS _
      (countableCompletionWeakIdealPresentation B S hS f hA J' hJ'dec hJ'zero) iso
  have hpres : HasSomeSurjectivePresentation B S hS X :=
    (hasAllSurjectivePresentations_of_weakIdealColimitPresentation B S hS
      (IdealSequenceLimit A J' hJ'dec) hwa hX pres).hasSomeSurjectivePresentation
  exact ⟨hpres, IdealSequenceLimit A J' hJ'dec, inferInstance,
    idealSequenceLimitTopology A J' hJ'dec, isTopologicalRing_idealSequenceLimit A J' hJ'dec,
    isLinearTopology_idealSequenceLimit A J' hJ'dec, ⟨hwa, ⟨pres⟩⟩, hQAdic, JQ, hJQdef, hJQfg⟩

/-- **Stacks 0APW (1).** Let `T ⊆ Spec A` be a closed set cut out by countably many equations
`e : ℕ → A`, and suppose the completion `X_{/T}` of `X = Spec A` along `T` is countably indexed,
in the sense that some decreasing sequence `J` of ideals cutting out `T` is cofinal among all
ideals cutting out `T`. Then `X_{/T}`, which is the colimit of the quotient spectra
`Spec (A ⧸ J n)`, is adic\*. The presenting ring is the inverse limit `lim A ⧸ J' n` along a
square-cofinal reindexing `J' = J ∘ idx` of `J`; passing to that subsequence does not change the
colimit, since the reindexing functor is final. -/
@[stacks 0APW "clause (1): a countably indexed completion whose closed set is cut out by \
countably many equations is adic star"]
theorem isAdicStar_countableCompletion (B : BigFppfSite.{u}) (S : Scheme.{u})
    (hS : B.Contains S) (f : Spec (.of A) ⟶ S) (hA : B.Contains (Spec (.of A)))
    {T : Set (PrimeSpectrum A)} (J : ℕ → Ideal A) (hJ : IsCofinalVanishingSequence A T J)
    (e : ℕ → A) (heT : T = PrimeSpectrum.zeroLocus (Set.range e)) :
    IsAdicStar B S hS (countableCompletion B S hS f hA J hJ.1) := by
  classical
  obtain ⟨idx, hmono, hidxle, hsq⟩ := exists_squareCofinalReindex J hJ
  obtain ⟨hJ'dec, hJ'zero, hJ'cofinal⟩ := hJ.comp_reindex hmono hidxle
  exact isAdicStar_of_squareCofinal B S hS f hA _ hJ'dec hJ'zero hJ'cofinal hsq e heT _
    (satisfiesSetTheoreticCondition_countableCompletion B S hS f hA J hJ.1 hJ.2.1)
    (countableCompletionReindexIso B S hS f hA J hJ.1 hmono hidxle hJ'dec).symm

end CountableCase

